# This is an illustrative example of a Tcl-like scrip to operate the C47/R47
# Commands used here:
#   nim for numerical entry. Not that you enter as per RPN entry, negative 4 is entered as RPN, using th CHS equivalent being -: nim 4 -
#   SIN or other commands are standard Tcl-like
#   xeq is a standard command that can be used to execute a loaded user function or a standard function. X! Is used below as standard function as well as print x
#   tsvfn to change the tav output file name: currently 10 char max including dot and extension. 

# This script was called:
#   ./c47 --headless  --script ./res/SCRIPTS/example.d47


nim 1.234
SIN
tsvfn fact12.tsv
xeq ⎙x

nim 451 
xeq x!
tsvfn fact12.tsv
xeq ⎙x

nim 0
nim 1.23
nim 66
xeq Xπ
xeq XMULT
nim 0
nim 1.23
nim 66
xeq XDIV

xeq x⇄y
tsvfn fact12.tsv
xeq ⎙x




